        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="waste" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="This module uses a mix of the previous inventory of an early design of a Swiss LAW repository and extrapolations using as a basis the current preliminary design of a Swiss SF, HLW, and ILW repository. No new design of a Swiss LAW repository has been designed yet. The module refers to the 100000 m3 LAW waste scenario. The early design consisted of a mined cavern system with horizontal access tunnels in an alpine region. After input of the waste, the remaining empty space of the tunnels is backfilled with concrete. To finally seal the repository, the access tunnels will also be refilled using the previously mined rock. Twenty percent of extracted rock is assumed to be disposed of in an inert material depository. The land use and reception building are assumed equal to the repository SF, HLW, and ILW. The use of industrial machines is estimated with the same assumptions as for repository SF, HLW, and ILW, with weight of tracks scaled down by the total lenght of the tunnels (4200 m). The total electricity supplied from the grid for the construction has been assumed equal to the total for the construction of the Swiss SF, HLW, and ILW repository, because the total mined volume is about the same and no information on the hosting rock is available. For completion the energy consumption for the past test drilling has also been included.;&#10;Synonyms: Low and intermediate level long-lived radioactive waste, Geological repository; &#10;UUID: b66757e1-ad06-3abc-bbba-ee21323b9d1d" includedProcesses="This module includes the material and energy requirements as well as transports for mining and refilling of shafts and tunnels of a repository for intermediate and long-lived low radioactive waste in the Swiss context. Also included is wastewater from mining and disposal of part of the mined rock. Land use of the entrance area and buildings are accounted for." infrastructureProcess="true" localCategory="waste" localName="Final repository for nuclear waste LLW" localSubCategory="nuclear waste\infrastructure" name="Final repository for nuclear waste LLW" subCategory="nuclear waste\infrastructure" unit="p"/>
